         score EVERY candidate at negative infinity, so Optimize handed back Score = -Infinity to
         callers that divide scores ("+x% from new drops"). A live probe found it. This suite could not.
         Extracting the search behind an explicit Inputs bag (pools keyed by GearLockSlot rather than
         the Assembly-CSharp `part` enum, cube/base/offhand/slot-counts/lookup passed in) is what makes
         "an infeasible floor set still returns a finite score" a test that can exist. -->
    <Compile Include="..\..\NGUAdvisor\Managers\GearSolver.cs" Link="Linked\GearSolver.cs" />
